    {
      "id": "1554754303107797074",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-30T07:18:31.799+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Oh, are you using the same script for LVS extraction and PEX extraction? Maybe you want to divide those, or at least use different magic scripts.\n\nBTW, I think the flattening above does NOT propagate lower hierarchy text to the top, so there's no problem with local naming of nets (if I understand your comment).\n\nThese are the commands that I use for hierarchical extraction for LVS.\n```\ndrc off\ncrashbackups stop\ngds drccheck off\nundo disable\nlocking disable\ngds flatten yes # flattens cells with less than 10 shapes\ngds flatglob <cellname> # repeated for other larger cells to be flattened before extracting. Note: All subcells must be explicitly flattened too.\ngds read <gdsfile>\nload <cellname>\nselect top cell\nexpand\nextract no all ;# clear all flags\nextract do aliases\nextract do local\nextract unique\next2spice lvs\next2spice merge conservative ;# reduce parallel devices\next2spice short resistor ;# keep both ports but connect them with a 0 ohm resistor\next2spice -o <cellname>.gds.spice <cellname>.ext\nfeedback save <cellname>.feedback.txt\n```\n\nFun fact: magic's default extraction connects virtual nets by name - disjoint nets with the same label are extracted as connected. \nUse `extract unique` to automatically add a `_uq*` suffix to unconnected duplicate labels.",
      "author": {
        "id": "738396032295108721",
        "name": "bailey8889",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "bailey",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-09_media/0-EB806.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
      "embeds": [],
